 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Future with werden",
     "texto": [
      "**werden** is conjugated and the main verb goes in the infinitive at the end: **Ich werde morgen anrufen** (I'll phone tomorrow). **Werden** can also express a forecast or assumption: **Es wird bald regnen** (it will probably rain soon). For plans already arranged, the present with a time expression is very common: **Morgen rufe ich dich an** (I'm calling you tomorrow). The future with **werden** doesn't by itself mean that a plan is more formal or more certain."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
